.TH MODBUSTER 1.SH NAMEmodbuster \- separate merged modules.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmodbuster\fR[\-qv] [\-b=size] [\-w=dir] file.SH DESCRIPTION\fBmodbuster\fRtakes a file of modules merged together -- a boot file, or anythingmade with\fBmerge\fRor\fBcat\fR-- and writes each module to a file of its own named after the module,in the current directory or the one\fB\-w\fRnames.  It separates relocatable files, BASIC09 source and K-Windowsbitmaps the same way.  It also leaves an empty file named\fB?\fRfor whatever follows the last module it recognises; remove it..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-w=\fIdir\fRwrite into\fIdir\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-b=\fIsize\fRthe buffer size..TP 12\fB\-q, \-v\fRquiet, or verbose..SH SEE ALSOdemerge, bsplt68